msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/wcmp-faq.php:167
msgid "Q: My changes aren't showing on the frontend. What should I do?"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/wcmp-faq.php:168
msgid "A: Try these steps:"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/wcmp-faq.php:170
msgid "Make sure you clicked \"Save Changes\" in the admin panel"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/wcmp-faq.php:171
msgid "Clear your browser cache and refresh the page"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/wcmp-faq.php:172
msgid "Clear any caching plugins (WP Super Cache, W3 Total Cache, etc.)"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/wcmp-faq.php:173
msgid "Check if the endpoint is enabled (power icon should be ON)"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/wcmp-faq.php:174
msgid "Verify user role restrictions aren't hiding the item"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/wcmp-faq.php:179
msgid "Q: I'm getting a 404 error on my custom endpoint. How do I fix it?"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/wcmp-faq.php:180
msgid "A: Go to WordPress Settings → Permalinks and click \"Save Changes\" without changing anything. This will flush the rewrite rules and make your endpoint accessible."
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/wcmp-faq.php:184
msgid "Q: Can I restore the default WooCommerce menu?"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/wcmp-faq.php:185
msgid "A: Yes, simply remove all custom endpoints, groups, and links, and leave only the default WooCommerce endpoints (Dashboard, Orders, Downloads, Addresses, Account Details, Logout). You can also deactivate the plugin temporarily to see the default layout."
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/wcmp-faq.php:189
msgid "Q: The drag and drop isn't working. What's wrong?"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/wcmp-faq.php:190
msgid "A: This is usually a JavaScript conflict. Try:"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/wcmp-faq.php:192
